## Step 6 — Sanity checks

```bash
CE="$REPO_ROOT/scripts/oci-local-dev/container-engine.sh"
# DBs
"$CE" exec vcp-postgres psql -U postgres -c '\l' | grep -E 'vcp|temporal|temporal_visibility'
# Temporal UI
curl -fsS http://localhost:8088/ >/dev/null && echo "Temporal UI reachable"
# vlm-worker registered as a poller on its task queue
"$CE" exec vcp-temporal sh -c \
  'temporal task-queue describe \
     --task-queue vsa-lifecycle-manager-9.18.1 \
     --namespace default \
     --address $(hostname):7233' \
  | grep -q UNVERSIONED && echo "vlm-worker registered with Temporal"
```

The published ports (`:5432`, `:7233`, `:8088`) are forwarded to the host
loopback, so the from-source `oci-proxy`/`vcp-worker` reach the stack at
`localhost` unchanged.

All three must pass before proceeding.

